From 7381bf3a779f077d70e956775a1e84b1c754dd76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:54:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] flashnext: the prompt tile runs two stages and two
 blocks an SM, and its launches are registered

The relaxed 128 x 128 prompt tile (TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_MX128, whose kernels came in with the
prefill lever) also runs as a two-stage, two-blocks-an-SM variant under TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_GEMM2=1:
one block's output stores and pipeline fill overlap the other block's K loop, at the three-stage
tile's bits (TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_GEMM2, off by default). The tile's four launches, three-stage and
two-stage, bf16 and fp32, carry their nvcc 13.0 sm_12x resource receipts (175 and 128 registers a
thread) in the contract's flashnext tile records, later compilers pending. The kv-cache fp8 launch
records return to flashnext_kv8_pending.zig (their symbols' kernels are in the stack): the file
had been reduced to its header, which left the contract chain without the records it imports.

Squash of stack commits 49ac1a495 and 4c368739f (port-0015-mx128 @ c747816f).
